{
  "title": "A server with node:http",
  "lesson": "js/07-http-and-servers",
  "kind": "http",
  "lang": "javascript",
  "edit": [
    "server.mjs"
  ],
  "start": [
    "node",
    "server.mjs"
  ],
  "start_timeout": 20,
  "requests": [
    {
      "name": "GET /health answers 200 with JSON",
      "path": "/health",
      "status": 200,
      "json": {
        "status": "ok"
      },
      "header": {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "GET /hello?name=Sam greets by name",
      "path": "/hello?name=Sam",
      "status": 200,
      "json": {
        "message": "Hello, Sam!"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "GET /hello without a name greets the world",
      "path": "/hello",
      "status": 200,
      "json": {
        "message": "Hello, world!"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "POST /echo sends the JSON body back",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/echo",
      "body": {
        "a": 1,
        "list": [
          "x",
          "y"
        ]
      },
      "status": 200,
      "json": {
        "a": 1,
        "list": [
          "x",
          "y"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "POST /echo with invalid JSON answers 400",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/echo",
      "headers": {
        "Content-Type": "text/plain"
      },
      "raw": "{not json",
      "status": 400,
      "json_contains": {
        "error": "invalid JSON"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an unknown path answers 404 with JSON",
      "path": "/nope",
      "status": 404,
      "json": {
        "error": "not found"
      },
      "header": {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the wrong method on a known path answers 404",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/health",
      "body": {},
      "status": 404
    },
    {
      "name": "the server is still running after the errors",
      "path": "/health",
      "status": 200
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Listen on process.env.PORT. The tests choose the port.",
    "const url = new URL(req.url, \"http://localhost\"); then url.pathname and url.searchParams.get(\"name\").",
    "Read the body with: let text = \"\"; for await (const chunk of req) text += chunk;",
    "Wrap JSON.parse in try/catch and answer 400 with { error: \"invalid JSON\" }."
  ]
}
